# Office Unbound ICS host: 80/443 are the public entry (owner's router forwards them here, 2026-11-20). Who may reach WHAT is decided by
# nginx: /etc/nginx/ou-public-sni.conf (443 by TLS server name: deployment names -> their VMs; the ICS console only from LAN/VPN, every other
# connection closed) and sites-enabled/ou-public-http.conf (80: deployment names only). Everything else on this host stays unreachable from
# outside as before (no other port is opened here).
table inet ics_admin {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority -10; policy accept;
    tcp dport { 80, 443 } accept
  }
}
